## 3. Reconciled audit verdict (frozen) — read once

A two-auditor parallel-truth run completed 2026-05-10. The reconciled verdict
overrides any single-auditor verdict.

### Master verdict

**PARTIAL** — most landed; 2 P1 wire breaks block the "22 plans complete"
claim. Acceptable for internal dogfooding; not acceptable for public release.

### Tally (post-reconciliation)

| Bucket | Count | Plan IDs |
|---|---:|---|
| PASS | 8 | 01, 02, 06, 09, 13, 15, 21 (post-backfill), 22 |
| PASS_WITH_GAPS | 10 | 03, 05, 07, 08, 10, 11, 12 (internal/downstream PARTIAL), 14, 18, 20 |
| PARTIAL | 1 | **04** (P1 — server twin-export emit/consume mismatch + client command not registered) |
| STAGE_PASS | 2 | 16 (Stage 1 substrate), 19 (Stage 1 extractors) — Stage 2 explicitly deferred by design |
| STAGE_PASS_WITH_GAPS | 1 | 17 (Stage 2 v2 incremental; R05 extractor-driven slice deferred to Plan 19) |
| FAIL | 0 | — |
| UNVERIFIED | 0 | — |

### Severity counts

| Tier | Count | Definition |
|---|---:|---|
| P0 | 0 | Catastrophic — breaks consumer at first use |
| P1 | **2** | Wire break — common consumer cannot complete the round-trip |
| P2 | 6 | Functional gap — degraded behavior or unbounded surface |
| P3 | 7 | Documentation / test density / minor cosmetic |

### The 10 cross-task patterns (context, not tasks)

1. **Emit-side vs consume-side string-literal mismatch.** Plan 04 server (twin-export emit ≠ mapping) + Plan 11 (`since_marker` emit ≠ since input).
2. **Frontmatter test-count claims vs reality.** Plan 14 claims 7 unit tests in `semantic.rs`, actual 3.
3. **Infrastructure deferred downstream adoption.** Plan 12 cursor wrap consumed only by Plan 14; 5/7/11/15 still emit unwrapped.
4. **Capability advertises surface that params struct doesn't carry.** Plan 18 advertises `symbol_id_version` on `loctree/aicx` but `AicxParams` has only string `target`.
5. **Forward-drift capability upgrades (positive).** Plan 20's `liveDocumentCache: true` (Plan 17 wired live cache) vs plan body's `false` — implementer saw further than spec.
6. **Stub-honesty pattern enforcement varies.** Plan 15 uses typed `unsupported(...)` envelopes (good); Plan 04 has aspirational mapping codes never emitted (anti-pattern).
7. **Test fixtures assert mapped-but-unproduced inputs.** Plan 04 tests use `"exact-twin"` (mapping accepts; diagnostics never emit).
8. **Plan 21 had no plan file** — backfilled in audit close-out session (CLOSED).
9. **Stub counters / dead enum variants in notifications.** Plan 10 `files_processed:0` hardcoded, `Composing` variant dead.
10. **LSP audits cannot stop at server scope.** Codex's parallel-truth catch on Plan 04 client-side proved this — future audits must `grep` server-advertised commands against editor client manifests.

