#### Task 24 · M · Polish HTML artifacts to loctree-com design system

- [ ] **Status:** open

**What's broken:** Plan 23 will ship a functional HTML artifact. Functional ≠ shippable to humans. Current `loctree-rs/src/analyzer/html.rs` uses ad-hoc inline CSS — no design system, no token discipline, no brand voice. When embedded in `loctree.com/cloud/teams/{slug}/reports/{fingerprint}/` (Plan 25+ on SaaS side), the report will feel like alien iframe content.

**Target state:** Adopt loctree-com's design system in the analyzer's HTML output.

**Visual contract (from `loctree-com/docs/design-system.md` + `BRAND.md`):**

Surface tokens (vendor `loctree-com/styles/tokens.css`):
- `--ink` `#0e0e0e` (page bg), `--ink2` `#161616` (alt sections), `--ink3` `#1e1e1e` (cards)
- `--bone` `#f5f1e7` (text), `--bone-dim` `rgba(245,241,231,0.86)` (body)
- `--teal` / `--amber` (accents — exact hex from loctree-com tokens.css)

Typography: serif display (h1/h2) + sans body + monospace UI labels (variable WOFF2, self-hosted from `reports/assets/fonts/`).

Authority-label badge color routing:
- `RepoVerified` → `--teal`
- `LoctreeDerived` → `--bone-dim`
- `AicxOperator` → `--amber`
- `AicxAgent` → `--bone-dim` muted with subtle border
- `AicxFailure` → red-amber from tokens
- `SemanticGuess` → `--bone-dim` with hatched border (heuristic warning)
- `StaleOrUnknown` → grayscale, struck-through

Anti-aesthetic gates (each MUST NOT appear in output):
- No pure black `#000` (use `--ink`).
- No gradients on surfaces.
- No glow / blur / drop-shadow ornament.
- No glass-morphism `backdrop-filter`.
- No CRT scanline overlay.
- No animated entrance / scroll-jack (CSS micro-transitions OK).

Mobile responsive at 375px viewport (Cytoscape collapses to "tap to view full graph"). Print stylesheet for "save as PDF." Contrast: AAA on body, AA on UI accents.

**Files to create / touch:**
- `reports/styles/tokens.css` (NEW, vendored from `loctree-com/styles/tokens.css`).
- `reports/styles/fonts.css` (NEW, vendored).
- `reports/styles/report.css` (NEW, report-specific extensions).
- `reports/assets/fonts/*.woff2` (NEW, vendored binary).
- `reports/src/components/authority_badge.rs` (NEW) — Leptos badge component.
- `reports/src/components/atlas_card.rs` — restyle.
- `reports/src/components/{semantic_facts,cross_language_coverage,manifest_footer}.rs` (from Task 23) — restyle.
- `loctree-rs/src/analyzer/html.rs` — purge hardcoded hex; inline CSS in `<style>` block.
- `reports/tests/visual_contract.rs` (NEW) — token + anti-aesthetic gate.

**Test contract:**
- `cargo test -p report-leptos --test visual_contract` asserts:
  - HTML output contains design-token CSS-var names (`--ink`, `--bone`, `--teal`).
  - HTML output does NOT contain hardcoded `#000000` / `#fff` / non-token hex.
  - HTML output does NOT contain `gradient-` / `backdrop-filter:` / `scanline` / `animation:.*entrance`.
- Manual smoke: open `/tmp/loctree-report-styled/index.html` in Safari + Firefox + Chrome; resize to 375px; Cmd+P to test print; visual diff against loctree.com landing.

**Cross-repo coordination:** This plan **consumes** but does **not modify** `loctree-com/styles/tokens.css`, `loctree-com/styles/fonts.css`, `loctree-com/public/fonts/*.woff2`. Vendoring is a snapshot copy, not a live dependency. Re-vendor per major brand decision.

**Non-goals:**
- No new analyzer behavior (Task 23 set the content; this task styles it).
- No SaaS-side surface changes.
- No JS-driven theming (single dark theme matching landing).
- No animations beyond CSS micro-transitions.
- No external CDN dependencies.
- No light-theme variant in v1.

**Complexity:** M (estimated 6-10h).

**Dependencies:** Task 23 (this styles what 23 emits).

